==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Bokoblin Horns are [[Monster Part]]s that are dropped by all types of [[Bokoblin]]s and [[Stalkoblin]]s upon defeat. They can be used with critters in a [[Cooking Pot]] to [[Cooking|Cook]] [[Elixir]]s.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> The [[Kochi Dye Shop]] accepts Bokoblin Horns as ingredients for [[Gray Dye]]. They can also be sold to [[Kilton]] at [[Fang and Bone]] for three [[Mon]].

Bokoblin Horns are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Bokoblin Horn}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Bokoblin Horn}}
Bokoblin Horns are [[Monster Horn]]s dropped by standard [[Bokoblin]]s and [[Stalkoblin]]s upon their defeat. Known for being sharp and barbed, they can be used when [[Cooking]] with critters at [[Cooking Pot]] or [[Portable Pot]] to create [[Elixir]]s.<ref name="TotK Inventory"/> When [[Fuse]]d to [[Weapon]]s, they increase the Weapon's attack power by four. When Fused to [[Shield]], they cause [[Link]]'s [[Parry|Parries]] to damage [[Enemy|Enemies]].

Bokoblin Horns are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Bokoblin Horn}}

